1
00:00:03,180 --> 00:00:04,890
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,350 --> 00:00:10,730
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:14,610
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,570 --> 00:00:17,410
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,860 --> 00:00:21,450
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:24,330
Now...

7
00:00:24,950 --> 00:00:26,630
...you are mine.

8
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:29,840
I don't give a damn about you.

9
00:00:31,390 --> 00:00:33,090
The rear guard will be...

10
00:00:33,650 --> 00:00:34,540
Guts...

11
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:35,840
I want you to do it.

12
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:40,430
Now it's my job to take care of the rest!

13
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:14,510
Feel no shame about shape

14
00:01:14,590 --> 00:01:16,430
Weather changes their phrase

15
00:01:16,550 --> 00:01:20,180
Even mother will show you another way

16
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:22,560
So put your glasses on

17
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:24,640
Nothing will be wrong

18
00:01:24,730 --> 00:01:26,850
There's no blame. There's no fame

19
00:01:26,850 --> 00:01:28,690
It's up to you

20
00:01:28,850 --> 00:01:32,320
The first words should be found

21
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:35,950
Whatever holds you back

22
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:37,320
I...

23
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:38,450
...can...

24
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:40,620
I can get it off

25
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:41,620
Tell me what...

26
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:42,620
Tell me what...

27
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:44,450
Tell me what you want

28
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:45,540
I don't know why...

29
00:01:45,750 --> 00:01:46,540
Don't know why...

30
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:48,540
Don't know why you're afraid

31
00:01:48,710 --> 00:01:49,710
Tell me what...

32
00:01:49,790 --> 00:01:50,670
Tell me what...

33
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,340
Tell me what you'd say

34
00:01:52,590 --> 00:01:53,670
I don't know why...

35
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:54,760
Don't know why...

36
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:55,550
Too late...

37
00:01:55,630 --> 00:01:57,170
It's too late

38
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:06,100
The Hand of God

39
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:36,010
Hey, you're up early.

40
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:39,300
You really like high places, don't you?

41
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:46,350
So? What's your take on us?

42
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:47,800
What do you mean?

43
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:49,700
You think it's the place for you?

44
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:51,440
I don't know yet.

45
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:54,270
It's different here...

46
00:02:54,730 --> 00:02:57,780
Everybody's the same
in ordinary mercenary bands.

47
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:03,070
It's easy to see their ranks are full of
hoodlums and men with shady pasts.

48
00:03:03,990 --> 00:03:06,620
But I think something's different here...

49
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:09,160
I wonder if that's true...

50
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:12,330
If I had to explain why,
I would say it's Griffith.

51
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,790
Everyone sincerely admires Griffith...

52
00:03:16,090 --> 00:03:20,090
Everyone expects great things
to come from staying with Griffith...

53
00:03:21,010 --> 00:03:25,470
To sum up, these men have gathered
because of Griffith's charisma.

54
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:28,770
Of course, it's kill or be killed...

55
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:31,270
We fight in bloody battles every day...

56
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:35,150
...but strange as it sounds,
we can live like normal people here.

57
00:03:35,610 --> 00:03:38,190
What kind of guy is Griffith really?

58
00:03:41,150 --> 00:03:42,150
I don't know.

59
00:03:43,570 --> 00:03:44,870
Now, now, listen...

60
00:03:45,410 --> 00:03:47,330
I can't really describe it, but...

61
00:03:47,330 --> 00:03:52,290
I think Griffith believes in something
beyond swordsmanship and tactics.

62
00:03:52,290 --> 00:03:57,130
It's probably beyond his reach to turn
his belief into reality in one lifetime.

63
00:03:57,130 --> 00:03:58,590
That's what he has.

64
00:03:58,960 --> 00:03:59,920
His belief?

65
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:00,460
In what?

66
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:02,340
In everything.

67
00:04:05,550 --> 00:04:06,970
Hey, rookie!

68
00:04:06,970 --> 00:04:08,010
Griffith's calling you!

69
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:10,390
See ya.

70
00:04:14,310 --> 00:04:15,230
Guts!

71
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:18,860
I bet you'll find it right here...

72
00:04:18,860 --> 00:04:21,190
...the place where you belong.

73
00:04:35,710 --> 00:04:36,830
Hey!

74
00:04:36,830 --> 00:04:38,710
What do you say? Join me!

75
00:04:38,710 --> 00:04:41,460
There's nothing better for a hangover.

76
00:04:41,460 --> 00:04:42,590
I'm fine.

77
00:04:42,590 --> 00:04:44,680
Oh, come on, don't be shy.

78
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:47,430
Cut it out! We're not kids,
for crying out loud!

79
00:04:50,390 --> 00:04:52,180
What a funny face!

80
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:57,400
Nice try!

81
00:05:11,660 --> 00:05:14,200
Awfully feisty for so early in the day.

82
00:05:19,290 --> 00:05:21,300
That was some good morning exercise.

83
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:25,760
Guts, you...

84
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:26,970
Now we're even.

85
00:05:32,810 --> 00:05:34,390
All right, I surrender.

86
00:05:34,850 --> 00:05:36,770
You are entirely too thickheaded.

87
00:05:39,610 --> 00:05:41,070
Oh, this?

88
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:44,690
I got this from an old
fortune-teller woman long ago.

89
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:46,900
The behelit...

90
00:05:46,900 --> 00:05:49,490
This is also known as the Egg of the King...

91
00:05:49,490 --> 00:05:53,040
...for once you possess this,
you are destined to rule the world...

92
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:55,370
...in exchange for your flesh and blood.

93
00:05:55,950 --> 00:05:57,370
Rule the world?

94
00:05:57,370 --> 00:05:57,870
Catch!

95
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:09,720
I don't know how it works though...

96
00:06:09,720 --> 00:06:11,800
It looks alive, doesn't it?

97
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:12,810
It's creepy...

98
00:06:14,810 --> 00:06:15,970
Isn't it fascinating?

99
00:06:19,650 --> 00:06:22,150
I didn't hear your answer yet.

100
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:26,530
Why did you come back
to help me during that battle?

101
00:06:26,990 --> 00:06:30,200
I didn't want to lose an outstanding
warrior like you in such trivial battle.

102
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:32,450
I put in so much work to get you.

103
00:06:36,910 --> 00:06:37,960
Guts...

104
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:39,670
You should come along with me.

105
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:42,630
Now we've taken only a step...

106
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:46,460
The Band of the Hawk itself...
Victory in several battles...

107
00:06:46,760 --> 00:06:49,260
It's merely the first step, just the beginning.

108
00:06:50,010 --> 00:06:52,140
The real fun for us has yet to come...

109
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:54,100
...and we're ready to risk our lives for it.

110
00:06:56,220 --> 00:06:58,350
I will have my own kingdom.

111
00:06:58,810 --> 00:07:00,770
You must fight for me...

112
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:03,520
...because you belong to me.

113
00:07:04,690 --> 00:07:07,690
I will choose the place
where you will die for me.

114
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:25,590
Have his own kingdom?

115
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:28,210
He's not nobility or royalty,
much less a knight...

116
00:07:28,210 --> 00:07:32,720
He's no more than the leader of
a mercenary band of 500 or so...

117
00:07:33,550 --> 00:07:37,100
But he talks as if all that is his right...

118
00:07:37,810 --> 00:07:39,770
The enemy numbers about a thousand.

119
00:07:40,060 --> 00:07:44,230
The first unit leads, while
the second and third cover the flanks!

120
00:07:44,810 --> 00:07:46,520
First unit, charge!

121
00:07:52,530 --> 00:07:55,820
What have I really been
doing for the past four years?

122
00:07:57,580 --> 00:07:58,950
Guts!

123
00:07:58,950 --> 00:07:59,790
Guts!

124
00:07:59,790 --> 00:08:00,700
Give me my spear!

125
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:02,460
Be quick about it!

126
00:08:09,460 --> 00:08:11,470
Don't be so damn slow!

127
00:08:11,470 --> 00:08:12,880
Do you want to get me killed?

128
00:08:17,350 --> 00:08:18,310
Gambino...

129
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:22,430
Come on, what are you doing?

130
00:08:23,350 --> 00:08:27,440
Hey, Guts, why not use a smaller
sword, one right for your size?

131
00:08:28,070 --> 00:08:29,020
Never!

132
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:31,530
You thickheaded brat!

133
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:40,120
We don't carry any swords
for kids here anyway!

134
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:42,830
Is it true the kid was born from a corpse?

135
00:08:42,830 --> 00:08:45,580
Yeah, Gambino's wife, Shisu, found him.

136
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:48,340
That's a sign of bad luck...

137
00:08:48,340 --> 00:08:50,750
Then it was probably
his fault Shisu died, right?

138
00:08:57,470 --> 00:09:00,970
It's only when I wielded this that I didn't
have to think about anything else.

139
00:09:01,270 --> 00:09:03,140
To the victor go all the spoils!

140
00:09:03,730 --> 00:09:04,640
Hey, Guts!

141
00:09:05,270 --> 00:09:07,270
It's your first real battle. Work hard.

142
00:09:08,810 --> 00:09:09,520
Charge!

143
00:09:44,930 --> 00:09:46,020
Gambino!

144
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:47,690
Watch your ass!

145
00:09:47,690 --> 00:09:49,020
This is not a swordplay lesson!

146
00:09:49,230 --> 00:09:51,230
Don't act like an idiot
just because you took one down!

147
00:10:02,530 --> 00:10:03,410
Next!

148
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:05,040
Gambino!

149
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:07,000
What's up?

150
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:09,790
Look!

151
00:10:14,460 --> 00:10:15,300
Here you go.

152
00:10:16,050 --> 00:10:17,760
Well, keep it up.

153
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:18,930
Yeah!

154
00:10:25,180 --> 00:10:26,270
Go!

155
00:10:26,270 --> 00:10:27,350
We're close!

156
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:29,140
Charge!

157
00:10:35,570 --> 00:10:36,360
Gambino!

158
00:10:41,030 --> 00:10:42,530
Gambino, look at this!

159
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:48,710
I got the enemy commander!

160
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:50,580
I won the whole reward!

161
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:52,420
What about meat?

162
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:54,130
Meat...

163
00:10:54,130 --> 00:10:55,630
...to feed him.

164
00:10:55,630 --> 00:10:56,670
O-Okay...

165
00:10:57,420 --> 00:10:58,880
What is it?

166
00:10:58,880 --> 00:11:00,090
Just bring me the meat...

167
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:01,840
Bring it right now!

168
00:11:06,720 --> 00:11:08,100
I'll go get it.

169
00:11:11,270 --> 00:11:14,020
He's got it good, our Gambino!

170
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:16,690
We should all follow his example.

171
00:11:16,690 --> 00:11:18,690
Hey, what did you say?

172
00:11:19,650 --> 00:11:21,200
What the hell did you say?

173
00:11:21,410 --> 00:11:23,070
J-Just kidding...

174
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:53,690


175
00:11:56,520 --> 00:11:57,480
Gambino?

176
00:12:04,450 --> 00:12:06,280
G-Gambino...

177
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:11,620
It's unlike me to be so careless...

178
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:14,500
I expected you to drop dead long ago.

179
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:16,380
You should be dead, bastard...

180
00:12:16,790 --> 00:12:18,210
And what happened?

181
00:12:18,210 --> 00:12:21,300
Shisu, who found you,
dropped dead instead...

182
00:12:21,300 --> 00:12:23,430
And now I'm in this miserable condition...

183
00:12:23,430 --> 00:12:26,090
This is like a joke!

184
00:12:27,180 --> 00:12:29,260
What do you have against me?

185
00:12:29,260 --> 00:12:31,060
You return good with evil!

186
00:12:31,350 --> 00:12:32,930
Gambino, I...

187
00:12:33,350 --> 00:12:35,810
You're a son of the devil.

188
00:12:35,810 --> 00:12:38,820
A doomed child raised under an evil sign...

189
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:41,530
You were the one who deserved to die...

190
00:12:41,940 --> 00:12:43,780
...on that day eleven years ago...

191
00:12:44,070 --> 00:12:46,280
...beneath your mother's body...

192
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:48,280
You should have died!

193
00:13:03,670 --> 00:13:06,300
You were never more than a pest.

194
00:13:06,590 --> 00:13:10,760
I hated you, following me around
like a dog after you killed Shisu.

195
00:13:12,140 --> 00:13:13,350
You...

196
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:15,440
...should have died!

197
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:23,400
Y-You killed...

198
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:27,660
Shisu...

199
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:34,750
G-Gambino...

200
00:13:42,750 --> 00:13:43,340
Gam...

201
00:13:47,590 --> 00:13:49,220
What's wrong? Night raid?

202
00:13:50,930 --> 00:13:52,060
Guts!

203
00:13:52,060 --> 00:13:53,390
What the hell is going on here?

204
00:13:53,680 --> 00:13:55,310
Don't tell me you did this...

205
00:13:56,770 --> 00:13:58,230
You, answer me!

206
00:14:00,810 --> 00:14:02,150
You did it...

207
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,280
Wait!

208
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:03,940
This isn't...

209
00:14:03,940 --> 00:14:05,440
You'll pay for this!

210
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:06,400
Get him!

211
00:14:14,830 --> 00:14:16,000
What happened?

212
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:16,750
What the...

213
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:18,080
It's Guts!

214
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:20,290
That kid just killed Gambino!

215
00:14:20,750 --> 00:14:22,000
You've got to be kidding!

216
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,130
It's true!

217
00:14:23,130 --> 00:14:26,970
The kid just bit the hand that
fed him for more than ten years!

218
00:14:26,970 --> 00:14:28,930
It's no different than murdering his father!

219
00:14:29,260 --> 00:14:30,300
Why?

220
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:31,600
Why did this happen?

221
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:34,720
Wait!

222
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:35,770
You murderer!

223
00:14:53,330 --> 00:14:54,740
Did we get him?

224
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:56,370
Yeah, I think so.

225
00:14:56,370 --> 00:14:58,910
Falling from this height
would mean certain death anyway.

226
00:14:59,330 --> 00:15:03,000
Either way, Gambino will never
be able to rest in the afterlife.

227
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:10,340
I can't move...

228
00:15:11,180 --> 00:15:13,260
My body is frozen...

229
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:15,970
Will I die here...

230
00:15:15,970 --> 00:15:17,180
Will I...

231
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:53,430
Where am I going?

232
00:15:53,930 --> 00:15:56,350
If I had stayed
back there, I'd be better off...

233
00:15:56,640 --> 00:15:58,720
If I were dead back there...

234
00:15:59,850 --> 00:16:01,810
There would be nothing more...

235
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:04,940
But now bad things are waiting...

236
00:16:05,730 --> 00:16:06,820
Where...

237
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:15,370
It's the end...

238
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:17,240
The end...

239
00:16:18,910 --> 00:16:20,200
Yes, this is...

240
00:16:39,260 --> 00:16:41,640
I have not changed at all from back then...

241
00:16:41,930 --> 00:16:43,560
Just killing enemies...

242
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:44,730
...only to survive...

243
00:16:45,100 --> 00:16:46,560
Where do I want to go?

244
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:47,230
Where...

245
00:17:00,370 --> 00:17:02,620
Hey, are you still alive?

246
00:17:02,620 --> 00:17:04,330
Yeah, I think so.

247
00:17:04,620 --> 00:17:07,080
You have the devil's own luck,
no matter what you do.

248
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:08,290
Here...

249
00:17:13,630 --> 00:17:18,140
On the battlefield, a soldier's life
is worth no more than a silver coin.

250
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:20,640
As if it were nothing...

251
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:24,480
...most men's lives are controlled
by a handful of nobles and royalty.

252
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:29,690
Well, even a king is really unable
to live his life as he pleases...

253
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:35,240
We're all just surrendering to
the flow that is known as fate...

254
00:17:36,150 --> 00:17:38,620
Then we fade away.

255
00:17:38,620 --> 00:17:42,410
Our lives are squandered,
and we don't know who we are.

256
00:17:43,870 --> 00:17:49,210
There must be a man who's born with
the leverage to change the world...

257
00:17:49,210 --> 00:17:51,840
...regardless of social status or class.

258
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:54,920
That man would be part of
this world's true privileged class.

259
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:57,260
That man could have
the absolute power of a god!

260
00:17:58,340 --> 00:17:59,760
I must know...

261
00:18:00,050 --> 00:18:02,720
...what my status really is in this world!

262
00:18:03,350 --> 00:18:06,390
What has been preordained for me in this life?

263
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:10,810
It's strange...

264
00:18:12,730 --> 00:18:16,030
I've never told this
to anyone else before, only you.

265
00:18:28,040 --> 00:18:29,040
Mr. Guts!

266
00:18:29,040 --> 00:18:29,960
Mr. Guts!

267
00:18:35,670 --> 00:18:37,340
What's your problem?

268
00:18:37,550 --> 00:18:40,180
I just wanted to congratulate you.

269
00:18:40,550 --> 00:18:44,560
Mr. Guts, I heard you were
promoted to raider commander.

270
00:18:44,560 --> 00:18:48,390
It's amazing. You only have
two weeks of experience.

271
00:18:48,390 --> 00:18:50,060
It's no big deal at all.

272
00:18:50,060 --> 00:18:51,230
Anyway...

273
00:18:51,230 --> 00:18:54,400
You've become one of us for real!

274
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:55,690
Congratulations!

275
00:18:57,570 --> 00:18:58,900
Just call me Guts.

276
00:19:06,450 --> 00:19:07,700
Pippin!

277
00:19:07,700 --> 00:19:08,910
Look, we fell!

278
00:19:08,910 --> 00:19:10,420
You should be careful!

279
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:12,880
What the hell do you think you're doing?

280
00:19:19,220 --> 00:19:23,640
In days long past,
beyond one's distant memories...

281
00:19:23,970 --> 00:19:28,520
...man has shielded the tiny wounds
in his heart by picking up a sword.

282
00:19:29,390 --> 00:19:33,730
In days yet to come,
beyond one's distant hopes...

283
00:19:34,060 --> 00:19:37,650
...man will wield a sword so
that he may smile upon his journey.

284
00:19:39,780 --> 00:19:42,530
A kingdom in the west
and an empire in the east.

285
00:19:42,950 --> 00:19:47,740
The war between Midland and Tudor
has lasted one hundred years.

286
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:51,460
During the war,
the Grim Reapers of the Battlefield...

287
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:52,920
...the Band of the Hawk...

288
00:19:52,920 --> 00:19:58,250
...increased their power greatly,
fighting on the side of Midland.

289
00:20:00,590 --> 00:20:02,380
Three years have passed...

290
00:20:03,510 --> 00:20:05,090
Charge, charge!

291
00:20:05,090 --> 00:20:06,470
Tear them apart!

292
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:18,650
We, the Black Ram Heavy Cavalry...

293
00:20:18,650 --> 00:20:20,900
...must lend our courage
to the entire empire!

294
00:20:20,900 --> 00:20:22,150
Kill them all!

295
00:20:22,150 --> 00:20:23,150
Crush them to pieces!

296
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:29,450
I can barely watch my men!

297
00:20:29,450 --> 00:20:33,370
They are thrown into confusion by
an army of only three thousand men!

298
00:20:33,670 --> 00:20:36,960
Due to our foes' onslaught,
we've endured immense damage!

299
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:39,090
We'll be cut off from the castle!

300
00:20:40,260 --> 00:20:42,130
I ask for anyone's help...

301
00:20:42,130 --> 00:20:45,970
I beseech anyone who can stop
the march of Tudor's black devils...

302
00:20:46,300 --> 00:20:48,300
Charge, charge!

303
00:20:57,650 --> 00:20:58,730
What nonsense!

304
00:20:58,730 --> 00:21:00,570
Fighting against us all by himself?

305
00:21:00,570 --> 00:21:01,690
All right!

306
00:21:01,690 --> 00:21:03,110
We'll shatter your bones!

307
00:21:19,380 --> 00:21:21,460
D-Don't break up your formation!

308
00:21:21,460 --> 00:21:22,920
Only one soldier is against us!

309
00:21:23,340 --> 00:21:24,470
Encircle him!

310
00:21:24,470 --> 00:21:25,590
Cut off his movements!

311
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:31,220
T-They are...

312
00:21:31,220 --> 00:21:32,850
Your Majesty, look!

313
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:34,560
T-The Band of the Hawk!

314
00:21:34,890 --> 00:21:38,560
The Grim Reapers of the Battlefield
led by the White Hawk, Griffith!

315
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

316
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

317
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

318
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

319
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

320
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

321
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

322
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

323
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

324
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

325
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

